{0 console}

Colours, tables, trees and progress rows for OCaml command-line tools.

[console] prints into the terminal's normal scrollback. While work runs it
redraws only the progress rows of a {!Console.Display}.

Its widgets lay out text in a style and print with
{{:https://erratique.ch/software/fmt}Fmt}. They are drawn in the colours
and the {!Console.Theme} of the formatter that prints them, and as plain
text on a pipe:

{@ocaml[
# let sizes =
    Console.Table.(
      v
        [
          column (Console.Span.text "Package");
          column ~align:`Right (Console.Span.text "Size");
        ]
        [
          [ Console.Span.text "console"; Console.Span.text "42 KiB" ];
          [ Console.Span.text "console-eio"; Console.Span.text "9 KiB" ];
        ]);;
val sizes : Console.Table.t = <abstr>
# Fmt.pr "%a@." Console.Table.pp sizes;;
╭─────────────┬────────╮
│ Package     │   Size │
├─────────────┼────────┤
│ console     │ 42 KiB │
│ console-eio │  9 KiB │
╰─────────────┴────────╯
- : unit = ()
]}

{1:manuals Manuals}

{ul
{- {{!page-widgets}Widgets and themes} shows the widgets with the text they
   print, and how the themes draw them.}
{- The [console-eio] package runs the progress rows with Eio. Its
   documentation opens with a tutorial, {i A first CLI}. It builds a whole
   command step by step, with options for colour and theme, a table,
   progress rows and a test of its output.}}

{1:libraries Libraries}

The [console] package has four libraries:

{ul
{- [console], the module {!Console}: styles, spans, the widgets, the themes
   and the live {!Console.Display}. It needs neither Eio nor Unix.}
{- [console.tty], the module {!Console_tty}: colour, colour depth and UTF-8
   for the standard outputs. It decides from the terminal and the
   environment, or from a [--color] option.}
{- [console.text], the module {!Console_text}: untrusted text made safe to
   print, without the rest of [console].}
{- [console.input], the module {!Console_input}: a line editor that turns
   the bytes typed into echo and lines. It does no input or output itself.}}

{1:start Where to start}

{ul
{- {!Console.Span} and {!Console.Style} for text in colour.}
{- {!Console.Table}, {!Console.Tree}, {!Console.Panel}, {!Console.Rule} and
   {!Console.Bar} for the widgets.}
{- {!Console.Theme} to choose a look, and to let users choose one with a
   [--theme] option.}
{- {!Console.Display} for the rules of the live rows: where text goes, what
   a pipe gets and what the display guarantees.}}
